# The Origin 300 sMDK matrix: one row per processor population, one column
# per standalone diagnostic. A cell is `run` or a reason key from
# lib_prom_smdk.REASONS saying why the population does not run it yet.
# lib_prom_smdk.DIAGS holds each diagnostic's arguments;
# test_prom_smdk_origin300.py and the test_prom_smdk_origin300_<row>.py
# beside it boot the stock PROM and the monitor once per diagnostic.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
#
# These eight are the Origin 300 set the project checkout's NOW.md derives
# from the sMDK field guide (108-0264-004, Tables 2-1 and 3-1) and the
# package's own diaglist. The router, IO7 and GSN programs decline for want
# of hardware the machine does not carry, and iocfg and topology are
# utilities with no verdict, so none of those has a column.
#
# budget is the seconds the whole row may take, test start to report;
# every wait is cut to what is left of it. meson.build gives each row's
# target 120s more.
#
# id | cpus | budget | sct | nmem | ndir | scct | CPU_Test | System_Level_Test | io8bt | xbg
